f Rome, Italy, and serves as the administrative centre of the Catholic Church. Vatican City is governed by the See of Rome, commonly known as the Holy See, itself a sovereign entity under international law, which maintains its temporal power, governance, diplomacy, and spiritual independence. Vatican is also used as a metonym for the Holy See, which is the central governing body of the Catholic Church and Vatican City, comprising the pope and the Roman Curia. The independent state of Vatican City came into existence in 1929 via the Lateran Treaty between the Holy See and the Kingdom of Italy, which spoke of it as a creation, not as a vestige of the much larger Papal States (756–1870), which had…","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_City","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"VA"}],"arc":{"reports":25,"first_seen":"2026-10-12T22:00:00Z","first_title":"Can you same-day register and vote on election day in California? What to know","first_url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","first_publisher":"Sacramento Bee","earlier":[{"id":"e_bbb8ae700c95","title":"Pope Leo requested mail ballot for Illinois midterms, says clerk","date":"2026-10-30T01:44:00Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxPSEFVdXVsLXdlcmFJd1VWUWU4bmhiQlptd2NjQVFCekFTYjJ4dkhnamNQQ183b3FjbFBseXVWNUJvU0tpY0FxTDdfNldhZl9ZQ0NZQkpPMHYweHByOWo1QnR3MWN5QXlrN2VhRnZZdGZzUVQ1RW9rTGJoNWFFREE2LWJ6OWJHSC03c1hEeUdxZ01BNWlsOGEzYm90YlFKRHZaU0NXYkRuMEJDN1ZUdGQ4Rw?oc=5","publisher":"Forbes","verification":"multi_source_reporting"},{"id":"e_b5327574ca2f","title":"Pope Leo XIV votes in US midterm elections via mail-in ballot","date":"2026-10-30T13:05:48Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxOSGI4NEdQS2kwQnA1cG1uLWJUaTIzOGQxUVRmenV0SWloUmxqcHdYRXhxejVVdnlUSG9EVTFFcmNmVGc4djQtSVVSVUMwTVpOQWlHOWhSVUlWN2RsZ05KcVprVEY3U3VlSllWRW5IaTl5WC0zQXFiVkdodkZZbm5Rc1ZhUUE0YlhPYms3YmFNczRkS0UxMDZHSw?oc=5","publisher":"Vatican News","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_9f